## Goal

Produce the canonical `docs/e2e-journeys/` catalog **on main** via the live non-gate Bashir path — the first real end-to-end exercise of the Bashir invocation machinery. Reconcile the prior scouting output (which lives on branch `bashir/phase-1-catalog`, authored outside the pipeline and now stale relative to main) against current main, and land it through the normal merge gate. This closes Phase 1 of the Bashir-onboarding workstream. Philipp signs off on the catalog after it lands (formal Phase 1 acceptance criterion).

## Context

Read these first:
- `.claude/roles/bashir/ROLE.md` — your anchor and operating contract.
- `.claude/roles/bashir/inbox/HANDOFF-PHASE-1-SCOUTING-BRIEF-FROM-DAX.md` — Dax's scouting brief. It is the authoritative spec for WHAT the catalog is: the two artifact classes (INDEX.md + one spec per journey), the mandatory per-journey frontmatter + section structure, the seven categories, and the catalog-completeness criterion.
- Your prior scouting output on branch `bashir/phase-1-catalog`: `INDEX.md` + 11 `J-*.md` specs under `docs/e2e-journeys/`. Pull each with `git show bashir/phase-1-catalog:docs/e2e-journeys/<file>`. This is YOUR earlier work — reconcile and refresh it against current main; do not start blind and do not blindly copy it.
- Scouting sources on current main: `docs/` (runbook, contracts), the Ops UI (`dashboard/lcars-dashboard.html` + Ziyal's redesign spec referenced in `.claude/roles/obrien/inbox/`), and the register/event surfaces. Catalog the intended user-facing flow, with the implementation as one input — not the spec.

Pre-condition: slice 303 merged (non-gate template anchor path fixed) — enforced via `depends-on`. `.claude/roles/bashir/ROLE.md` resolves from the corrected template path.

## Scope

- Author `docs/e2e-journeys/INDEX.md` listing every journey (ID, one-line description, category, status, source-doc citations), browseable in one screen.
- Author one spec file per journey at `docs/e2e-journeys/J-<kebab-case>.md` following the mandatory frontmatter (`id`, `category`, `status`, `last_reviewed`) and sections (What the user is trying to accomplish, Preconditions, Steps, Expected outcomes, Known failure modes, Sources, Open questions).
- Reconcile the 11 prior specs against current product state: keep, correct, add, or retire journeys as the current main warrants.
- Cover every category at least once: `authoring-staging`, `dispatch-execution`, `review-verdict`, `gate-merge`, `recovery`, `observability`, `direct-controls`. Cover every Ops panel and every slice's user-facing effect.

## Out of scope

- Writing or running regression tests (Phase 2+).
- Running the regression gate; touching `gate-telemetry`, `branch-state.json` gate state, or `DS9_USE_GATE_FLOW`.
- Any code changes. Catalog is docs-only.

## Acceptance criteria

- `docs/e2e-journeys/INDEX.md` exists and lists every journey with ID / description / category / status / source-doc citation.
- Every journey has a `docs/e2e-journeys/J-<kebab>.md` spec with the mandatory frontmatter and all required sections.
- Every one of the seven categories has at least one journey.
- Gaps, contradictions, or inconsistencies found while scouting are recorded in each spec's "Open questions" — not papered over.
- All `status:` fields are `draft` (Philipp's sign-off later elevates them; do not self-mark `signed-off`).

## Quality + goal check

A Phase-2 test author can take any single spec file and write a regression test from the AC/Expected-outcomes text alone, without reading the implementation.

## Tasks

1. Read your ROLE.md and Dax's scouting brief.
2. Pull the prior catalog from `bashir/phase-1-catalog`; diff it against current main.
3. Scout current main (docs, Ops UI, register/event surfaces).
4. Author/refresh `INDEX.md` + per-journey specs to the mandatory structure.
5. Record findings as "Open questions" inside the relevant specs.
6. Commit the catalog to the slice branch (docs-only changeset).

## Constraints

- Docs only — all changes under `docs/e2e-journeys/`. Zero code, zero gate-state writes.
- AC-blind discipline per ROLE.md: the catalog reflects the intended user-facing flow; the implementation is one input, not the source of truth.
- Maintain your heartbeat per the non-gate prompt template for the duration of the run.
